<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <title>ShopEase Privacy Policy</title>
    <style>
        :root{font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:#292324;background:#faf6f4;line-height:1.65}
        *{box-sizing:border-box}
        body{margin:0}
        header{background:#52070b;color:#fff;padding:28px max(22px,calc((100% - 980px)/2))}
        header a{color:#fff}
        main{max-width:980px;margin:30px auto;padding:0 22px 50px}
        h1,h2,h3{line-height:1.25;color:#651319}
        h1{color:#fff;margin:0 0 6px}
        h2{margin-top:34px}
        .version,.notice{font-size:.92rem;color:#65595a}
        .notice{border-left:4px solid #d47a67;background:#fff;padding:14px 18px;margin:22px 0}
        section{background:#fff;border:1px solid #eee2df;border-radius:10px;padding:20px 24px;margin:18px 0}
        li{margin:7px 0}
        footer{margin-top:30px;font-size:.9rem;color:#65595a}
        @media(max-width:600px){section{padding:16px}header{padding:22px}}
    </style>
</head>
<body>
<header>
    <h1>ShopEase Privacy Policy</h1>
    <div>How ShopEase handles personal information across users.</div>
</header>
<main>
    <p class="version">Privacy Policy version: {{ $privacyVersion }} · Effective November 15, 2026</p>
    <div class="notice"><strong>Before registering:</strong> Read this Policy and separately acknowledge it on the registration form. Your acknowledgment records that the Policy was presented; it does not waive your rights under the Data Privacy Act of 2012 (Republic Act No. 10173), its implementing rules, or other applicable law.</div>

    <section>
        <h2>1. Who this Policy covers and who handles your information</h2>
        <p>This Policy applies when you visit or use ShopEase, create or apply for an account, place or fulfill an order, communicate with another user, process a return or complaint, manage a wallet or settlement, or perform a logistics, rider, courier, hub, or sorting-center task.</p>
        <p>The ShopEase platform operator acts as the personal information controller for information it decides to collect and use to operate the platform. Sellers and logistics partners may separately act as controllers for information they process for their own legal and service obligations. Providers that host or support ShopEase may act as personal information processors under their service arrangements. The operator's complete registered legal name and Data Protection Officer contact should be published here before launch; contact <a href="mailto:support@shopease.com">support@shopease.com</a> for privacy questions in the meantime.</p>
        <p>This Policy is written for a Philippine e-commerce and delivery service and is intended to be read with the ShopEase Terms and Conditions, including the role-specific terms accepted during registration.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>2. Philippine privacy and related laws</h2>
        <p>ShopEase will handle personal information in accordance with the Philippine laws and rules that apply to the particular processing and transaction. The core privacy framework includes:</p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Republic Act No. 10173, the Data Privacy Act of 2012 (DPA).</strong> This is the primary Philippine statute governing personal information processing by public and private entities. Relevant provisions include Section 11 (general data privacy principles), Sections 12 and 13 (criteria for lawful processing of personal information and sensitive personal information), Section 16 (data subject rights), Section 20 (security of personal information), and Section 21 (accountability for transfer of personal information). <a href="https://lawphil.net/statutes/repacts/ra2012/ra_10173_2012.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read RA 10173 on LawPhil</a>.</li>
            <li><strong>Implementing Rules and Regulations of RA 10173.</strong> The IRR gives effect to the DPA's requirements, including transparency, legitimate purpose, proportionality, lawful processing, retention, data sharing, security, and data subject rights. Applicable National Privacy Commission (NPC) circulars, rules, and guidance on matters such as security and personal data breach notification must also be followed as relevant. <a href="https://privacy.gov.ph/implementing-rules-regulations-data-privacy-act-2012/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read the DPA IRR on the NPC website</a>.</li>
            <li><strong>Republic Act No. 11967, the Internet Transactions Act of 2023.</strong> Its consumer and merchant protections apply to covered internet transactions and include recognition of data privacy as part of the e-commerce framework. It complements—but does not replace—the DPA. <a href="https://lawphil.net/statutes/repacts/ra2023/ra_11967_2023.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read RA 11967 on LawPhil</a>.</li>
            <li><strong>Republic Act No. 8792, the Electronic Commerce Act of 2000.</strong> Its rules on electronic data messages, documents, and transactions may apply to ShopEase's electronic records and communications. It does not replace the DPA's requirements for personal information. <a href="https://lawphil.net/statutes/repacts/ra2000/ra_8792_2000.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read RA 8792 on LawPhil</a>.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>The DPA and its IRR are the principal privacy authorities for the practices described in this Policy. The application of each other law depends on the specific transaction and ShopEase's legal obligations; this list is not a legal opinion or a complete list of every law that may apply. Mandatory legal rights prevail over any inconsistent platform term.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>3. Personal information ShopEase may collect</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Account and identity details:</strong> name, email address, phone number, date of birth, age, sex, password credential (stored as a password hash), account role, registration status, account security and verification records, and profile photo if supplied.</li>
            <li><strong>Address and business information:</strong> home, business, delivery, service-area, branch, and hub addresses; business or store name and category; company and authorized representative details; and information about service areas and operations.</li>
            <li><strong>Verification and registration documents:</strong> identity documents; business permits and registrations; tax or company information submitted in registration; driver's license; vehicle and plate details; OR/CR where requested; representative authorization; insurance or courier-authority documents; and related application status and review notes. These documents can contain sensitive personal information and are used only for the relevant verification and operational purposes.</li>
            <li><strong>Orders and transactions:</strong> products, quantities, order history, prices, voucher use, shipping details, payment method and status, refund and return requests, wallet credits and debits, seller settlement and commission records, COD collection/remittance records, rider earnings entries, and transaction references. ShopEase should not receive or store full payment-card credentials through the currently implemented wallet flow.</li>
            <li><strong>Delivery and location information:</strong> recipient name, phone number, delivery address, tracking number, parcel scan and handoff history, delivery status, timestamps, route or manifest information, and proof-of-pickup, proof-of-delivery, return, or failed-attempt photos. When a rider uses the location-update feature, device-provided latitude/longitude and update time may be processed for assigned delivery tracking.</li>
            <li><strong>Messages, complaints, and support:</strong> messages exchanged through platform communication features, complaint details and outcomes, evidence files, return/dispute records, support tickets, and communications with administrators, sellers, logistics personnel, riders, or couriers.</li>
            <li><strong>Technical and security information:</strong> session and authentication data, verification/reset records, and information needed to protect the service and diagnose errors. Password-reset records may include the requesting IP address and user-agent information. The browser may also send ordinary request and device information to the application or its hosting provider.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Provide only information requested for your role and use the appropriate complaint or support channel for sensitive documents. Do not send passwords, one-time codes, or unrelated sensitive information in a message.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>4. Why ShopEase processes information</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>To create and administer accounts; verify identity, email, business authority, permits, and delivery qualifications; review applications; and maintain account security.</li>
            <li>To display products and shops; accept and manage orders; coordinate payment method, wallet activity, seller settlement, refunds and returns; and provide order, complaint, and support functions.</li>
            <li>To arrange parcel pickup, delivery, hub/center transfers, routing, tracking, failed-delivery or return handling, proof records, COD reconciliation, and logistics reporting.</li>
            <li>To send necessary service messages, verification codes, registration and account-status notices, order updates, security alerts, and responses to complaints or support requests.</li>
            <li>To investigate suspected fraud, unsafe conduct, privacy incidents, disputed transactions, missing or damaged parcels, policy violations, and score or account decisions; to enforce platform terms; and to protect users and ShopEase.</li>
            <li>To meet legal, regulatory, tax, accounting, recordkeeping, law-enforcement, and dispute-resolution obligations, and to establish, exercise, or defend legal claims.</li>
            <li>To maintain, troubleshoot, and improve the platform and its reliability. ShopEase should use aggregated or de-identified information for analysis where it is reasonably possible to do so.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>ShopEase processes information on applicable lawful bases, which may include performance of a contract or steps requested before a contract, compliance with legal obligations, legitimate interests that are not overridden by your rights, and consent where required by law. Sensitive personal information is processed only on a basis permitted by the Data Privacy Act and other applicable requirements. Where processing relies on consent, you may withdraw it subject to legal and contractual limits; withdrawal does not retroactively invalidate earlier lawful processing.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>5. When information is shared</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Buyer, seller, and delivery coordination:</strong> A seller receives the order details needed to prepare and fulfill the buyer's purchase. The assigned logistics partner, delivery hub, sorting center, rider, or courier receives the recipient, address, contact, parcel, route, and proof information needed for its assigned handoff or delivery. A buyer may see relevant seller and delivery status details. Access should be limited to the information needed for that task.</li>
            <li><strong>Logistics operations:</strong> Authorized logistics companies and their assigned centers or personnel may receive information needed to register staff, allocate routes, scan and reconcile parcels, review delivery actions, settle COD, or investigate operational disputes.</li>
            <li><strong>Administrators and support:</strong> Authorized ShopEase staff may access account, transaction, complaint, communication, and delivery records when needed for support, verification, operational review, fraud prevention, safety, compliance, or account enforcement.</li>
            <li><strong>Legal and safety disclosures:</strong> Information may be disclosed where required by law, valid legal process, a competent authority, or to protect users, prevent fraud or serious harm, investigate an incident, or establish or defend legal claims. ShopEase will limit the disclosure to what is reasonably necessary and lawful.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>ShopEase does not sell personal information. It does not disclose delivery or identity information for an unrelated recipient's marketing. A seller or logistics partner that receives information may have its own legal responsibilities and privacy notice for its separate processing.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>6. Storage, retention, and deletion</h2>
        <p>ShopEase retains information only for as long as reasonably necessary for the purposes above, including the life of an account and related services, transaction and accounting records required by law, open complaints and returns, fraud or safety reviews, security records, and the establishment or defense of legal claims. When information is no longer needed, it should be deleted, securely disposed of, or irreversibly de-identified, subject to legal holds and lawful retention requirements.</p>
        <p>You may ask to correct or delete account information. Deletion may be delayed or limited where ShopEase or another controller must retain information to complete an order, resolve a complaint, prevent fraud, meet a legal obligation, protect another person's rights, or establish or defend a claim. ShopEase will explain any applicable limitation when responding to a request.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>7. Cookies, sessions, and location</h2>
        <p>ShopEase uses session and authentication mechanisms, including browser session cookies where enabled, to keep a user signed in, protect account flows, and maintain necessary application state. Blocking these cookies may prevent sign-in, registration, or other functions from working. ShopEase does not describe advertising or analytics cookies here because no such use is identified as a required ShopEase feature in this Policy; if they are introduced, this Policy and any required consent controls should be updated first.</p>
        <p>The rider location feature may process the location coordinates supplied by a rider's device while the rider uses the feature for an assigned delivery task. Location is used for operational tracking and should be enabled only as needed for the assigned task. Stop sharing through the app or device when the task is complete, where the feature permits it.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>8. Security and incident response</h2>
        <p>ShopEase is responsible for maintaining reasonable organizational, physical, and technical safeguards appropriate to the sensitivity of the information, the risks of the processing, and applicable law. Users and business partners must protect credentials, limit access to authorized personnel, use personal information only for assigned purposes, and report suspected account compromise, document exposure, parcel-data disclosure, or other privacy incidents promptly.</p>
        <p>No online service can guarantee absolute security. If a personal data breach occurs, ShopEase will investigate, contain and document the incident, assess its risks, take appropriate remedial steps, and notify affected data subjects and the National Privacy Commission when required by law and applicable rules.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>9. Your privacy rights and choices</h2>
        <p>Subject to the Data Privacy Act and its implementing rules, you may have the right to be informed; access your personal information; object to or withdraw consent from certain processing; request correction or erasure/blocking where justified; request data portability where applicable; and be indemnified for damages caused by inaccurate, incomplete, outdated, false, unlawfully obtained, or unauthorized use of information. These rights are subject to legal conditions and exceptions.</p>
        <p>To make a privacy request, email <a href="mailto:support@shopease.com">support@shopease.com</a> from the email associated with your account and include your name, role, the request, and enough information to verify your identity. Do not email identity documents unless ShopEase requests them through a secure method. ShopEase may need to verify your identity, clarify the request, or explain a lawful reason for refusing or limiting it. You may also lodge a complaint with the National Privacy Commission or another competent authority under applicable law.</p>
        <p>To protect your account, use the account settings or support channel to update inaccurate contact or profile details. Requests to close an account do not automatically erase records ShopEase is legally required to retain or information needed to complete pending orders, settlement, or dispute handling.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>10. Minors and information about other people</h2>
        <p>ShopEase registration is intended for adults aged 18 or older. Do not register a child or provide a child's personal information except where lawful and necessary and with any authorization required by law. If you believe a minor's information was submitted improperly, contact ShopEase support so it can be reviewed.</p>
        <p>If you submit another person's information—for example, a recipient, business representative, or authorized contact—you must have authority to provide it and must give that person appropriate notice. Use recipient details only to complete the relevant order or delivery.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>11. Policy changes and privacy contact</h2>
        <p>ShopEase may update this Policy to reflect changes to its features, processing, providers, or legal requirements. The current version and effective date will be published here. Material changes will be brought to users' attention and, where required, renewed acknowledgment will be requested before continued use of affected services. The currently recorded acknowledgment includes the version and date/time for that account.</p>
        <p>For privacy questions or requests, contact <a href="mailto:support@shopease.com">support@shopease.com</a>. ShopEase's legal operator name and designated Data Protection Officer contact must be added to this Policy before production use.</p>
    </section>

    <footer>Related document: <a href="{{ route('terms-and-conditions') }}">ShopEase Terms and Conditions</a>. This Policy describes platform practices and does not limit rights under the Data Privacy Act of 2012 (Republic Act No. 10173) or other applicable law.</footer>
</main>
</body>
</html>
